  ${D}┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐${N}
  ${D}│${N}
  ${D}│${N}   ${C}HEIMDALL${N} ${D}(your machine)${N}
  ${D}│${N}       │
  ${D}│${N}       ├── local-1..4  ${D}(Heimdall sessions)${N}
  ${D}│${N}       │
  ${D}│${N}       ├── SSH ──→ ${R}asgard${N}-1..4  ${D}(Realm)${N}
  ${D}│${N}       └── SSH ──→ ${R}tatooine${N}-1..4  ${D}(Realm)${N}
  ${D}│${N}                       ▲
  ${D}│${N}                       │
  ${D}│${N}                    ${Y}📱 Raven${N}
  ${D}│${N}                    ssh → bifrost gateway
  ${D}│${N}
  ${D}└──────────────────────────────────────────┘${N}

${B}STEP 1 — CHECK PREREQUISITES${N}

  ${Y}\$${N} ${G}bifrost doctor${N}

  Checks: tmux, SSH, Tailscale (and iTerm2 on macOS).
  Tells you exactly what's missing and how to install it.

${B}STEP 2 — DISCOVER YOUR MACHINES${N}

  ${Y}\$${N} ${G}bifrost realm scan${N}

  Lists every machine on your Tailscale network.
  Shows which are already added as realms.

${B}STEP 3 — ADD REALMS${N}

  ${Y}\$${N} ${G}bifrost realm add asgard${N}

  Auto-detects the Tailscale hostname, tests SSH,
  copies your SSH key if needed, and syncs tmux.conf.
  The name you give it becomes the session prefix:
    asgard → ${D}asgard-1, asgard-2, asgard-3, asgard-4${N}

${B}STEP 4 — LAUNCH${N}

  ${Y}\$${N} ${G}bifrost workspace${N}

  ${D}On macOS + iTerm2:${N}
    Opens one iTerm window per realm, each with a 2x2 grid.
    Heimdall = black bg. Each realm = a different color.

  ${D}On Termux / Linux:${N}
